# Client Architecture

## One-way dependencies

```
app (pages)  ──▶  features  ──▶  shared
                  (features may use shared; shared must NEVER import features)
```

```
app/                 thin routes + layout + route handlers boundary only
features/<domain>/   coach (and future domains)
    api/             HTTP helpers (no logic/UI)
    components/      nest by concern + barrel `index.ts` (desk/, board/, composer/, check-in/, ui/)
    hooks/  stores/  utils/
    types/           ALL feature types + barrel `index.ts` (domain + i18n catalogs)
    index.ts         PUBLIC API — the only thing other slices may import
shared/              domain-agnostic ONLY
    components/  hooks/  utils/  constants/  lib/  types/
styles/              named CSS homes (never under components/) — e.g. coach-desk.css
```

- No feature code bloated into `app/page.tsx`. Pages compose features and read route params only.
- **`shared/` importing `@/features/...` is the #1 forbidden smell.**
- Cross-feature: `@/features/<domain>` (`index.ts`) only — never deep subpaths.
- **Inside a feature: relative imports only** (`./` / `../`). Never `@/features/<self>/…`.

## Thin pages

Pages compose feature components. No forms, mutations, domain toasts, or fetch orchestration in `app/page.tsx` — push into a feature hook/component.

## Separation of concerns

Components render JSX. Hooks decide. Utils compute (pure). Api fetches. Stores hold state.

| Concern | Where |
|---|---|
| Mutations / coach turns | `hooks/useXxx.ts` |
| Pure transforms | `utils/…` (no toast/navigate/network/hooks) |
| HTTP calls | `features/<domain>/api/…` |
| Global client state | `stores/…` (zustand) |

No data fetching, `.then()` chains, or business logic in a component body — extract to a hook.

## Types — strict placement

- Only type in a `.tsx`: its own `type Props = {…}` above the component.
- Domain models → `features/<domain>/types.ts`. Shared → `shared/types/`.
- Never export a reusable type from a component/hook file.
